const intro={"n":11,"title":"Cruz's New Fight at a Dance and Life as a Fugitive","summary":"Cruz continues telling his story. He compares the flow of his verses to sheep emerging from a pen, then recalls wandering as a fugitive. At a crowded rural dance, a guitarist sings teasing verses. Cruz reacts angrily, cuts the guitar strings, darkens the room and clashes with the musician. The man is gravely wounded; Cruz escapes into the countryside. He ends by reflecting bitterly on how authorities and communities treat an unfortunate gaucho.","people":"Sergeant Cruz, who continues his first-person narration; the guitarist whose verses he takes as insults; women and other guests at the dance; an armed foreign-born man who briefly appears.","themes":"Singing as storytelling; wounded pride; escalation and serious injury; flight and dispossession; the narrator's selective self-defense.","words":"coplas (short sung verses); pericón (traditional dance); pulpería (rural store and meeting place); guitarrero (guitar player); matrero (fugitive gaucho); pajales (tall grassy places).","questions":["Which imagery does Cruz use for the flood of words that starts his song?","How does the guitarist's teasing turn into violence?","What specifically does the text say about the musician's wounds, and does it explicitly record a death?","How do the crowded dance and sudden darkness change the encounter?","What similarities and differences can you identify between Cruz's dance episode and Fierro's earlier fights?"],"nums":[324,338,343],"analysis":"The singer's jokes are hurtful to Cruz, but his decision to cut the guitar strings and use violence is not inevitable. The text describes the injured singer's terrible wound without explicitly recounting his death here; a summary should not add one. Reading this canto alongside Fierro's violent dance scene reveals how both narrators frame their own actions through insult, fear and social persecution.","related":"/en/students/canto-7/","relatedTitle":"Compare Fierro's earlier violence at a dance"};
